      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142926",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/42/42dfc0c653fdcaf4f354ad1dfdf019406286e50dced6143bd4cb63770259a304.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 25$ from a normal population. Given that the sample variance is $s^{2} = 2$, find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population variance $\u03c3^{2}$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(X > 39.364) = 0.025$ and $P(X < 12.401) = 0.025$, where $X\u223c\u03c7^{2}(24)$ has a chi-square distribution with $24$ degrees of freedom, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
