      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143149",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ca/ca1fddd0d4cd9ad59ed551bb7c01811fb71e6b9d9d759a1ff7dc0b26c138958d.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n = 9$ from a normal population. Given that the sample variance is $s^{2} = 4$, find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population variance $\u03c3^{2}$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(X > 21.955) = 0.005$ and $P(X < 1.344) = 0.005$, where $X\u223c\u03c7^{2}(8)$ has a chi-square distribution with $8$ degrees of freedom, as shown in the diagram above.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
